From b174f771f1eb02d7b6756df743d84b2056eaff8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:38:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 40/43] WIP: power: regulator: pwm: use the channel from the
 pwms specifier

pwm_regulator_of_to_plat() reads the period and polarity from the pwms
specifier but never the channel, so pwm_id stays zero and the regulator
always drives channel 0 of its PWM controller. Boards whose regulator is
on the second channel, such as VDDCPU on PWM_J of the Khadas VIM1S, had
their init voltage programmed into the wrong channel.

Read the channel from the first specifier cell.

Fixes: 1a01695615f9 ("power: regulator: add pwm regulator")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/regulator/pwm_regulator.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/regulator/pwm_regulator.c b/drivers/power/regulator/pwm_regulator.c
index 7e73957f607..8e6cbfb381b 100644
--- a/drivers/power/regulator/pwm_regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/power/regulator/pwm_regulator.c
@@ -102,6 +102,7 @@ static int pwm_regulator_of_to_plat(struct udevice *dev)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	priv->pwm_id = args.args[0];
 	priv->period_ns = args.args[1];
 	priv->polarity = args.args[2];
 
